Q18: Write a program that accepts a percentage (0-100) and assigns a grade based on the following criteria: 
90-100: Grade A 
80-89: Grade B 
70-79: Grade C 
60-69: Grade D 
below 60: Grade F.

#include<stdio.h>
int main()
{ int m;

printf("enter the marks in percentage\n",m);
scanf("%d",&m);
if(m>=90&&m<=100)
{printf("grade A");}
else if(m>=80&&m<=89)
{printf("grade B");}
else if(m>=70&&m<=79)
{printf("grade C");}
else if(m>=60&&m<=69)
{printf("grade D");}
else 
{printf("grade F");}

}
